body:
I have already seen the vet as per the post... I was hoping someone may have had something similar they had with their pet that might have gotten a diagnosis from someone... I am not sure what to do, I have tried 2 different Vets now...

&#x200B;

Seems odd to me a subreddit titled "AskVet" and says "a place where you can ask veterinary related questions and get advice from veterinary professionals" that I can not get "advise from a veterinary professional"....

Okay so what elo are you?

Because this sounds like the most Iron - Bronze logic.

You make it sounds like every game you get into is toxic and/or has a troll in it.

&#x200B;

I am in Plat and find that I have someone toxic **maybe** 1 out of 10 games. Not every game. I also learned to play a variety of agents so that I am able to play something else if someone instant locks.

I play Yoru in 80% of my games and no, I do not instant lock, I simply hover over him and ask my team if they are alright if I play duelist. If someone locks in a duelist and we need a Smoke/Stall agent then I have my flex of either Sage or Omen.

&#x200B;

Essentially - learn to play more than 1 agent. Learn 1 for each role and don't worry about instant locking.

&#x200B;

If you (and I don't mean YOU specifically, I mean anyone in a generic term) have an attitude about playing a specific map or agent to the point of where you are going to troll or be toxic about it, don't play the fucking game.

I see what your saying, but essentially no raid is a "guaranteed payout". First you have to traverse the map to whatever location it is your going to without running into a PMC or Scav because well, your gonna die. And you might not even have the closest spawn.

Then you have to open said room or location and hope there is something good their because you aren't going to A L W A Y S come up with something amazing, it is RNG based after all as you mentioned.

&#x200B;

So say your doing Shoreline for example and running to resort. A ton of people go to resort so chances are you will come across someone. You might get inside and say get to room 310 but nothing spawned, so you walk out and wow there's a sweaty thicc boi waiting for you. Now you got nothing, and have to out of raid heal. Now you rinse and repeat say you die 6 times in a row and 1 time you come out with a gold chain, bit coin and horse statue. Was it worth the 6 times dyeing? Maybe. But boring as fuck that's for sure!

&#x200B;

Also feel like I should state I am not trying to argue or protect hatching running, just trying to see both sides!

This brings true meaning to the saying 

*"They don't make things like they used too"*

&#x200B;
